{"id": "EUVD-2026-103791", "enisaUuid": "1010f167-c67f-3b55-bb1c-f95072af54df", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfilter: nft_flow_offload: drop flowtable reference on init error path\n\nnft_flow_offload_init() bumps the flowtable use count with\nnft_use_inc() before calling nf_ct_netns_get().  When the latter\nfails, the error is returned as-is and the reference is leaked.\n\nThe upper layers do not balance it either: nf_tables_newexpr()\nclears expr->ops when the expression init callback fails, so the\nnft_expr_more() iteration in nft_rule_expr_deactivate() and\nnf_tables_rule_destroy() stops right before the failed expression\nand its ->destroy callback, which would drop the reference, never\nruns.\n\nEach failed rule addition therefore leaks one flowtable reference\nand the flowtable can no longer be removed: NFT_MSG_DELFLOWTABLE\nkeeps reporting -EBUSY even though no rule references it.\n\nSave the nf_ct_netns_get() return value and undo the nft_use_inc()\nwhen it fails, restoring the inc/dec pairing within\nnft_flow_offload_init() itself.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:50:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:57:30", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1d27214fd9a4d2c0c6d998fc9d4fb61448a3438e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/64ac0cb574c740bf723affb79b646eeba920db6b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c5f91098edee98c015f78488460a0609e62582a5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4cd378423a33194a773c267fc58606d28fce95cf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/747928b5d4ff8c8de55138a54c13980e4bb88578"], "aliases": ["GHSA-95vh-jxqc-h2w9", "CVE-2026-98851"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1bace249-4779-35eb-90a7-884995bd2c83", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "35bfd201-578f-308a-96da-b81feccc7586", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a3c90f7a2323b331ae816d5b0633e68148e25d04 <747928b5d4ff8c8de55138a54c13980e4bb88578"}, {"id": "3de0389e-06aa-31c7-9a8f-9535e487586f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "4a714cb2-85ae-364d-8834-9cf2a14946d4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "5348b866-c0f6-3b02-b30a-928ff1b61ed0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "876c88a9-ed7e-37b5-8338-1c050207cfd2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a3c90f7a2323b331ae816d5b0633e68148e25d04 <64ac0cb574c740bf723affb79b646eeba920db6b"}, {"id": "a723dc01-5e8a-368d-bb0b-7eed132102a5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a3c90f7a2323b331ae816d5b0633e68148e25d04 <4cd378423a33194a773c267fc58606d28fce95cf"}, {"id": "ae33d1bf-1b1b-3a7f-a438-b8ee8a991afd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a3c90f7a2323b331ae816d5b0633e68148e25d04 <c5f91098edee98c015f78488460a0609e62582a5"}, {"id": "d47ad9c3-f5a7-381b-938b-acf2c0d96b67", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "ea604603-c949-3014-8d26-016346ab1dd3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "f7b319d6-6f15-311b-a846-4c93ea84c475", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.16"}, {"id": "f845c9de-3c67-3d78-80bc-507c32fc3c86", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a3c90f7a2323b331ae816d5b0633e68148e25d04 <1d27214fd9a4d2c0c6d998fc9d4fb61448a3438e"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "bb5129a3-b5b8-3a51-a44e-f49374491b90", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}